d:[["$","header",null,{"className":"topbar is-detail","children":[["$","$L8",null,{"className":"brand","href":"/","children":"JOSE HERNANDEZ"}],["$","$L8",null,{"className":"link back","href":"/#work","children":"← ALL WORK"}],["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"hide-m","children":"PROJECT "}],"03"," / ","04"]}]]}],["$","main",null,{"children":[["$","section",null,{"className":"d-hero","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"stripe","aria-hidden":"true"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"d-ghost cond","aria-hidden":"true","children":"3"}],["$","h1",null,{"className":"cond","children":"Data Loss Prevention"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Scans Confluence pages and attachments every 10 minutes for exposed login details, personal data, and classified content."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"meta","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"label","children":"ROLE"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"meta-v","children":"Lead Engineer"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"label","children":"SHIPPED"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"meta-v","children":"09.2025"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"label","children":"STACK"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"meta-v","children":"Oracle APEX · PL/SQL · Oracle Text · ORDS"}]]}],null]}],["$","$L18","dlp",{"project":{"slug":"dlp","title":"Data Loss Prevention","tag":"DLP","year":"2025","shipped":"09.2025","role":"Lead Engineer","summary":"Scans Confluence pages and attachments every 10 minutes for exposed login details, personal data, and classified content.","stack":["Oracle APEX","PL/SQL","Oracle Text","ORDS"],"links":[],"sections":[{"label":"Overview","file":"README.md","command":"cat README.md","output":[{"text":"# Data Loss Prevention","tone":"accent"},"Finds exposed login details, personal data, and classified content in Confluence pages and attachments, then gets it fixed.","",{"text":"# all content stays in-house","tone":"dim"}],"prose":"Confluence is a shared workspace where teams write pages and upload files. Those pages and files can hold login details, personal data, or content marked confidential, and nothing was checking them. The content also had to stay in-house, so sending it to an outside scanning service wasn't an option."},{"label":"Approach","file":"plan.txt","command":"cat plan.txt","output":["[1] read pages and files in confluence","[2] scan new edits every 10 minutes","[3] look for sensitive data and keywords","[4] double-check matches to cut noise","[5] auto-restrict the clear-cut cases","[6] email authors, escalate if ignored"],"prose":"The company ran its own copy of Confluence, so the scanner could read pages and attachments directly. Every 10 minutes it checks only what was created or changed since the last run. When a match is almost certainly real, the system restricts access to the content and emails the author right away. Everything else waits for a person to review and confirm it."},{"label":"Architecture","file":"arch.txt","command":"cat arch.txt","output":["confluence",{"text":" |  pages + attachments","tone":"dim"}," v","scan new edits  (every 10 min)",{"text":" |  read text inside attachments","tone":"dim"},{"text":" |  look for sensitive data, keywords","tone":"dim"},{"text":" |  double-check each match","tone":"dim"}," v","match --> logged as an issue"," |"," +-> high confidence"," |    +-> restrict access"," |    +-> email author now"," |"," +-> everything else"," |    +-> human review queue"," |    +-> email author if confirmed"," v","author fixes via self-service link",{"text":"# no fix: reminders, then manager","tone":"dim"}],"prose":"The scanner first pulls the text out of attachments, so a file can be checked the same way as a page. It then looks for known patterns and keywords, and follow-up checks weed out false alarms. The same app lets the team manage the rules and follow results on dashboards. Authors get a self-service page, linked from the email, where they confirm their fix."},{"label":"Outcome","file":"results.log","command":"tail results.log","output":[{"text":"✓ thousands of issues caught in a year","tone":"accent"},{"text":"✓ hundreds of thousands of pages covered","tone":"accent"},{"text":"✓ ~15% false alarms","tone":"accent"},{"text":"✓ new content scanned every 10 min","tone":"accent"},{"text":"# unfixed issues escalate to managers","tone":"dim"}],"prose":"Over a year it caught thousands of issues across tens of thousands of Confluence spaces and hundreds of thousands of pages, and roughly 15% of its flags were false alarms. Authors who didn't fix flagged content got reminders, and issues that stayed unresolved went to their managers."},{"label":"Stack","file":"deps","command":"cat deps","output":["+ Oracle APEX","+ PL/SQL","+ Oracle Text","+ ORDS",{"text":"4 dependencies","tone":"dim"}],"prose":"Oracle APEX is a platform for building apps inside an Oracle database, so the scanner and the data it handled stayed in one place. The Oracle tools listed here covered the rest: reading attachments, searching text, connecting to Confluence, sending emails, and running scans on a schedule."}],"no":"03"}}],"$L19"]}],"$L1a"]
